@instanceA = http://localhost:5001
@instanceB = http://localhost:5002

### Create an expert with capacity 1
POST {{instanceA}}/api/experts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara", "capacity": 1, "topics": ["finance", "legal"] }

### Submit a request: assigned straight away
POST {{instanceA}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestKey": "demo-1", "topic": "finance", "title": "Invoice query", "priority": "Normal" }

### Retry the same key on the other instance: 200, the same request
POST {{instanceB}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestKey": "demo-1", "topic": "finance", "title": "Invoice query", "priority": "Normal" }

### The expert is full, so this one waits
POST {{instanceA}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestKey": "demo-2", "topic": "finance", "title": "Refund", "priority": "Normal" }

### An urgent request overtakes the normal one
POST {{instanceA}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestKey": "demo-3", "topic": "legal", "title": "Contract", "priority": "Urgent" }

### A topic nobody handles waits, and blocks nothing
POST {{instanceA}}/api/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestKey": "demo-4", "topic": "technical", "title": "Outage", "priority": "Urgent" }

### The queue, in service order
GET {{instanceA}}/api/requests/pending

### Close the first request: the urgent one is assigned next
POST {{instanceB}}/api/requests/1/close

### Check the expert
GET {{instanceA}}/api/experts/1
